{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7vb33pbFJKUM64GsZyq14","type":"tool_result","content":"779\t4. **Wait for all agents in wave to complete.**\n780\t\n781\t   **Plan-complete heartbeat (#2410):** as each executor returns (or is verified\n782\t   via spot-check below), emit one line — `complete` advances `{P}`, `failed`\n783\t   and `checkpoint` do not but still warm the stream:\n784\t\n785\t   ```\n786\t   [checkpoint] phase {PHASE_NUMBER} wave {N}/{M} plan {plan_id} complete ({P}/{Q} plans done)\n787\t   [checkpoint] phase {PHASE_NUMBER} wave {N}/{M} plan {plan_id} failed ({P}/{Q} plans done)\n788\t   [checkpoint] phase {PHASE_NUMBER} wave {N}/{M} plan {plan_id} checkpoint ({P}/{Q} plans done)\n789\t   ```\n790\t\n791\t   **Completion reconciliation (EVERY runtime — any spawn whose terminal response may not arrive):**\n792\t\n793\t   If a spawned agent does not return a normal terminal completion response — or its session ends abnormally (interrupted, aborted, closed, killed, timed out, `turn_aborted`, including ends the orchestrator itself initiated) — do NOT block indefinitely and do NOT classify the plan as failed yet. Read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/completion-reconciliation.md` — reconcile the plan artifacts FIRST, classify SECOND: SUMMARY present AND matching recent commits → complete (proceed to step 5, do NOT re-dispatch); no completion evidence → the failure handler. Verify, never wait.\n794\t\n795\t   **Configurable stall surveillance (#3212):** Every `${EXECUTOR_STALL_INTERVAL_MINUTES}`\n796\t   minutes while waiting, inspect `git log \"${EXPECTED_BRANCH}\" --since=\"${DISPATCH_TS}\"`\n797\t   for activity. If no completion signal, no SUMMARY.md, and no expected-branch\n798\t   commits appear for `${EXECUTOR_STALL_THRESHOLD_MINUTES}` minutes, pause and\n799\t   ask for one recovery path: `continue waiting`, `kill and retry`, or\n800\t   `kill and switch to inline execution`.\n801\t\n802\t   **A working executor is never steered (#4218).** The threshold measures time WITHOUT\n803\t   PROGRESS, not total runtime. Before treating an executor as stalled — and before sending it\n804\t   any message — read and execute `execute-phase/steps/executor-progress-policy.md`.\n805\t\n806\t5. **Post-wave hook validation (parallel mode only):** Hooks run on every executor commit by default (#2924); this post-wave run only fires when `workflow.worktree_skip_hooks=true` opted out of per-commit hooks:\n807\t   ```bash\n808\t   SKIP_HOOKS=$(gsd_run query config-get workflow.worktree_skip_hooks --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"false\")\n809\t   if [ \"$SKIP_HOOKS\" = \"true\" ]; then\n810\t     # Stash uncommitted changes under a named ref so we always pop (bare `git stash` strands them on hook/script failure). #3542: `refs/stash` is shared across worktrees, so this helper runs ONLY in the orchestrator's main checkout after all wave worktrees have been merged + removed; executors are forbidden from running any `git stash` subcommand (see `<destructive_git_prohibition>` in `agents/gsd-executor.md`).\n811\t     STASHED=false\n812\t     if (! git diff --quiet || ! git diff --cached --quiet) && git stash push -u -m \"gsd-post-wave-hook-$$\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then STASHED=true; fi\n813\t     git hook run pre-commit 2>&1 || echo \"⚠ Pre-commit hooks failed — review before continuing\"\n814\t     [ \"$STASHED\" = \"true\" ] && (git stash pop >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"⚠ Could not pop gsd-post-wave-hook stash — recover manually\")\n815\t   fi\n816\t   ```\n817\t   If hooks fail: report the failure and ask \"Fix hook issues now?\" or \"Continue to next wave?\"\n818\t\n819\t5.5. **Worktree cleanup (when `isolation=\"worktree\"` was used):**\n820\t\n821\t   **Standard wave contract:** Each wave's worktrees merge to main via the templated path below before the next wave's worktrees fork. The cleanup loop runs once per wave at the end of the wave lifecycle. Worktrees created in wave N must be fully removed before wave N+1 forks new ones.\n822\t\n823\t   **Cross-wave dependency deviation (supported execution mode):** When the orchestrator legitimately deviates from the standard wave model — for example, a phase with cross-wave plan dependencies that requires custom inter-worktree base-update merges (e.g., `merge: bring 09-01 + 09-02 into 09-03 base`) — the cleanup loop below is NOT automatically re-entered for those custom merges. The deviation path produces correct final history but bypasses this loop, leaving `worktree-agent-*` directories in place. Use the **cleanup-tail snippet** below to remove any residual worktrees after such a deviation.\n824\t\n825\t   When executor agents ran in worktree isolation, their commits land on temporary branches in separate working trees. After the wave completes, merge these changes back and clean up:\n826\t\n827\t   **Manifest source of truth (#3384):** Cleanup consumes the `WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST` created and populated during executor dispatch in step 3. Do not recreate or truncate it here.\n828\t\n829\t   Prefer the bounded helper, which validates branch identity, expected base, deletion\n830\t   diffs, merge result, and worktree removal before deleting the temporary branch.\n831\t   If the helper reports a blocked cleanup, resolve the reported manifest entry and\n832\t   rerun the same command. Do not fall back to broad worktree discovery.\n833\t\n834\t   ```bash\n835\t   [ -n \"${WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST:-}\" ] && [ -f \"$WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST\" ] || {\n836\t     echo \"BLOCKED: missing WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST; refusing broad worktree cleanup (#3384).\" >&2\n837\t     exit 1\n838\t   }\n839\t\n840\t   # Guard: pin cleanup back to the orchestrator's OWN worktree and fail on branch drift (#3174, #630).\n841\t   # Resolve from the dispatch-time orchestrator root persisted in the manifest — NOT `git worktree\n842\t   # list`'s first entry, which is always the main checkout and would pin a non-primary (per-phase\n843\t   # lane) orchestrator off its own branch, tripping the #3174 assertion below (#630). Byte-identical\n844\t   # for a primary orchestrator (its root IS the first entry); the fallback covers pre-#630 manifests.\n845\t   PRIMARY_WT=$(MANIFEST=\"$WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST\" node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");try{const j=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.env.MANIFEST,\"utf8\"));if(j&&j.orchestrator_root)process.stdout.write(String(j.orchestrator_root))}catch(e){}')\n846\t   [ -n \"$PRIMARY_WT\" ] || PRIMARY_WT=$(git worktree list --porcelain | awk '/^worktree /{print substr($0,10); exit}')\n847\t   if [ -z \"$PRIMARY_WT\" ]; then\n848\t     echo \"FATAL: could not resolve orchestrator worktree before cleanup\" >&2\n849\t     exit 1\n850\t   fi\n851\t   if [ -n \"$PRIMARY_WT\" ] && [ \"$(pwd -P 2>/dev/null)\" != \"$(cd \"$PRIMARY_WT\" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P)\" ]; then echo \"⚠ Orchestrator CWD drifted to $(pwd) — pinning to $PRIMARY_WT before worktree cleanup (#3174)\"; cd \"$PRIMARY_WT\" || { echo \"FATAL: cannot cd to primary worktree $PRIMARY_WT\" >&2; exit 1; }; fi\n852\t   ORCH_BRANCH=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)\n853\t   [ -z \"${EXPECTED_BRANCH:-}\" ] || [ \"$ORCH_BRANCH\" = \"$EXPECTED_BRANCH\" ] || { echo \"FATAL: orchestrator on '$ORCH_BRANCH' but expected '$EXPECTED_BRANCH' before worktree cleanup — refusing to merge (#3174-class drift)\" >&2; exit 1; }\n854\t\n855\t   # Fail closed: SDK refusal (safety guard #3174/#3384) must surface — do not swallow exit 1.\n856\t   gsd_run query worktree.cleanup-wave --manifest \"$WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST\" || exit 1\n857\t   ```\n858\t\n859\t   **Cleanup-tail snippet (use after any wave whose merges did not flow through the templated path above):**\n860\t\n861\t   If the orchestrator deviated from the standard wave merge path (e.g., custom inter-worktree base-update merges with `merge: bring …` style messages), run this snippet after the custom merges are complete. It reads only `WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST`; do not discover unrelated `worktree-agent-*` worktrees.\n862\t\n863\t   ```bash\n864\t   # Cleanup-tail: pin orchestrator CWD to its OWN worktree before cleanup-tail (#3174, #630).\n865\t   # Same fix as the templated path: resolve the dispatch-time orchestrator root from the manifest,\n866\t   # not `git worktree list`'s first entry (always the main checkout — wrong for a lane orchestrator).\n867\t   PRIMARY_WT=$(MANIFEST=\"$WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST\" node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");try{const j=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.env.MANIFEST,\"utf8\"));if(j&&j.orchestrator_root)process.stdout.write(String(j.orchestrator_root))}catch(e){}')\n868\t   [ -n \"$PRIMARY_WT\" ] || PRIMARY_WT=$(git worktree list --porcelain | awk '/^worktree /{print substr($0,10); exit}')\n869\t   if [ -n \"$PRIMARY_WT\" ] && [ \"$(pwd -P 2>/dev/null)\" != \"$(cd \"$PRIMARY_WT\" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P)\" ]; then echo \"⚠ Orchestrator CWD drifted to $(pwd) — pinning to $PRIMARY_WT before cleanup-tail (#3174)\"; cd \"$PRIMARY_WT\" || { echo \"FATAL: cannot cd to primary worktree $PRIMARY_WT\" >&2; exit 1; }; fi\n870\t   # Cleanup-tail: remove residual agent worktrees after a cross-wave-dependency deviation.\n871\t   # Uses only the current wave manifest to avoid touching unrelated active agents (#3384).\n872\t   WT_PATHS_FILE=$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gsd-worktree-paths-XXXXXX\")\n873\t   node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");const p=process.env.WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST;try{if(!p)throw new Error(\"WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST is unset\");if(!fs.existsSync(p))throw new Error(\"manifest does not exist\");const s=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\");if(!s.trim())throw new Error(\"manifest is empty\");const j=JSON.parse(s);for(const w of j.worktrees||[])if(w.worktree_path)console.log(w.worktree_path)}catch(e){console.error(`ERROR: cannot read worktree manifest ${p||\"(unset)\"}: ${e.message}`);process.exit(1)}' > \"$WT_PATHS_FILE\" || { echo \"BLOCKED: cannot read WAVE_WORKTREE_MANIFEST; refusing cleanup (#3384).\" >&2; exit 1; }\n874\t   while IFS= read -r WT; do\n875\t     [ -z \"$WT\" ] && continue\n876\t     WT_BRANCH=$(git -C \"$WT\" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null)\n877\t     [ -z \"$WT_BRANCH\" ] || [ \"$WT_BRANCH\" = \"HEAD\" ] && continue\n878\t     echo \"Cleaning up residual worktree: $WT (branch: $WT_BRANCH)\"\n879\t     git worktree unlock \"$WT\" 2>/dev/null || true\n880\t     if ! git worktree remove \"$WT\" --force; then\n881\t       WT_NAME=$(basename \"$WT\")\n882\t       if [ -f \".git/worktrees/${WT_NAME}/locked\" ]; then\n883\t         echo \"⚠ Worktree $WT is locked — unlock failed; manual cleanup required:\"\n884\t         echo \"    git worktree unlock \\\"$WT\\\" && git worktree remove \\\"$WT\\\" --force && git branch -D \\\"$WT_BRANCH\\\"\"\n885\t       else\n886\t         echo \"⚠ Residual worktree at $WT — remove failed; manual cleanup required\"\n887\t       fi\n888\t     else\n889\t       git branch -D \"$WT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || true\n890\t     fi\n891\t   done < \"$WT_PATHS_FILE\"\n892\t   git worktree prune\n893\t   ```\n894\t\n895\t   **When to skip step 5.5:**\n896\t\n897\t   **If no plan in this wave used worktree isolation** (project-level `USE_WORKTREES=false` OR every plan in the wave had `USE_WORKTREES_FOR_PLAN=false` — i.e. `WAVE_WORKTREE_PLANS` from step 2.5 is empty): all agents ran on the main working tree — skip this step entirely.\n898\t\n899\t   **If the orchestrator merged via custom messages (cross-wave-dependency deviation):** the templated cleanup loop above was not triggered for those merges. Run the cleanup-tail snippet above instead. After the snippet completes, proceed to step 5.6.\n900\t\n901\t   **If at least one plan used worktrees but others did not:** still run this cleanup — it iterates over actual `git worktree list` output and only merges back the worktrees that were created, leaving sequential plans' commits on the main tree untouched.\n902\t\n903\t   **If no worktrees found at runtime:** Skip silently — agents may have been spawned without worktree isolation, or the orchestrator already cleaned them up.\n904\t\n905\t   If the user declines to merge a worktree or a worktree over-reached scope, apply the worktree recovery policy (`execute-phase/steps/worktree-recovery-policy.md`) — never default to editing `main`.\n906\t\n907\t5.6. **Post-merge build & test gate:**\n908\t\n909\t   After merging all worktrees in a wave (parallel mode), or after the last plan completes\n910\t   (serial mode), run a build and then the project's test suite to catch cross-plan\n911\t   integration issues that individual worktree self-checks cannot detect (e.g., conflicting\n912\t   type definitions, removed exports, import changes, link errors).\n913\t\n914\t   This addresses the Generator self-evaluation blind spot identified in Anthropic's\n915\t   harness engineering research: agents reliably report Self-Check: PASSED even when\n916\t   merging their work creates failures.\n917\t\n918\t   Read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/post-merge-gate.md`.\n919\t\n920\t5.7. **Post-wave shared artifact update (when at least one plan used worktrees, skip if tests failed):**\n921\t\n922\t   When **any** executor agent in this wave ran with `isolation=\"worktree\"`, that agent skipped STATE.md and ROADMAP.md updates to avoid last-merge-wins overwrites. The orchestrator is the single writer for these files. After worktrees are merged back, update shared artifacts once for every completed plan in the wave (worktree-mode plans **and** sequential plans that ran on the main tree but deferred to the orchestrator for tracking writes).\n923\t\n924\t   **Only update tracking when tests passed (TEST_EXIT=0).**\n925\t   If tests failed or timed out, skip the tracking update — plans should\n926\t   not be marked as complete when integration tests are failing or inconclusive.\n927\t\n928\t   ```bash\n929\t   # Guard: only update tracking if post-merge tests passed\n930\t   # Timeout (124) is treated as inconclusive — do NOT mark plans complete\n931\t   if [ \"${TEST_EXIT}\" -eq 0 ]; then\n932\t     # Update ROADMAP plan progress for each completed plan in this wave\n933\t     for plan_id in {completed_plan_ids}; do\n934\t       gsd_run query roadmap.update-plan-progress \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" \"${plan_id}\" \"complete\"\n935\t     done\n936\t\n937\t     # Only commit tracking files if they actually changed\n938\t     if ! git diff --quiet .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md 2>/dev/null; then\n939\t       gsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-${PHASE_NUMBER}): update tracking after wave ${N}\" --files .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md\n940\t     fi\n941\t   elif [ \"${TEST_EXIT}\" -eq 124 ]; then\n942\t     echo \"⚠ Skipping tracking update — test suite timed out. Plans remain in-progress. Run tests manually to confirm.\"\n943\t   else\n944\t     echo \"⚠ Skipping tracking update — post-merge tests failed (exit ${TEST_EXIT}). Plans remain in-progress until tests pass.\"\n945\t   fi\n946\t   ```\n947\t\n948\t   Where `WAVE_PLAN_IDS` is the space-separated list of plan IDs that completed in this wave.\n949\t\n950\t   **If no plan in this wave used worktrees** (project-level `USE_WORKTREES=false` OR `WAVE_WORKTREE_PLANS` is empty): sequential agents already updated STATE.md and ROADMAP.md themselves — skip this step.\n951\t\n952\t5.75. **Execute:wave:post capability dispatch:**\n953\t\n954\t   After worktree merge, post-merge tests, and tracking updates, dispatch capability hooks registered at `execute:wave:post`. The primary hook is the `ui.safety-gate` gate from the UI capability — it verifies that any frontend files changed in this wave conform to the UI-SPEC contract.\n955\t\n956\t   ```bash\n957\t   WAVE_POST_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:wave:post --raw)\n958\t   ```\n959\t\n960\t   Read the `activeHooks` array from `WAVE_POST_HOOKS_JSON` in-context (do NOT pipe through a shell parser).\n961\t\n962\t   **If `activeHooks` is empty or absent:** Skip silently to step 5.8.\n963\t\n964\t   **Contribution dispatch:** inject every `kind == \"contribution\"` fragment per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md (skip when none), before the gates below.\n965\t\n966\t   **Step dispatch:** dispatch every `kind == \"step\"` hook per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md (skip when none) — not one shape of one. A step here is advisory: it never blocks wave completion. ⚠ **Validate `ref.command` in-context before any shell use** (third-party manifest input) — loop-hook-dispatch.md § `step`. **`ref.skill == \"code-review\"` (#3661):** the generic contract's bare skill dispatch carries no phase argument, but `code-review.md`'s `initialize` step requires one (`PHASE_ARG=\"${1}\"`) or it reports \"Phase not found\" and exits — pass it explicitly, mirroring step `code_review_gate` in `execute-phase/steps/verify-phase-goal.md`: `Skill(skill=\"gsd-code-review\", args=\"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")`.\n967\t\n968\t   **For each active entry where `kind == \"gate\"`** (process in array order): read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/wave-post-gate-hooks.md` for the full evaluation contract (check validation, `onError`, blocking semantics, mapper spawn). A gate declared `blocking: false` — the `drift` capability's codebase-drift gate is one — is non-blocking by contract: it reports and the wave continues. When all active gates are processed without a blocking halt, continue to step 5.8.\n969\t\n970\t5.8. **Handle test gate failures (when `WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT > 0`):**\n971\t\n972\t   ```\n973\t   ## ⚠ Post-Merge Test Failure (cumulative failures: ${WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT})\n974\t\n975\t   Wave {N} worktrees merged successfully, but {M} tests fail after merge.\n976\t   This typically indicates conflicting changes across parallel plans\n977\t   (e.g., type definitions, shared imports, API contracts).\n978\t\n979\t   Failed tests:\n980\t   {first 10 lines of failure output}\n981\t\n982\t   Options:\n983\t   1. Fix now (recommended) — resolve conflicts before next wave\n984\t   2. Continue — failures may compound in subsequent waves\n985\t   ```\n986\t\n987\t   Note: If `WAVE_FAILURE_COUNT > 1`, strongly recommend \"Fix now\" — compounding\n988\t   failures across multiple waves become exponentially harder to diagnose.\n989\t\n990\t   If \"Fix now\": diagnose failures (import conflicts, missing types,\n991\t   or changed function signatures from parallel plans modifying the same module).\n992\t   Fix, commit as `fix: resolve post-merge conflicts from wave {N}`, re-run tests.\n993\t\n994\t   **Why this matters:** Worktree isolation means each agent's Self-Check passes\n995\t   in isolation. But when merged, add/add conflicts in shared files (models, registries,\n996\t   CLI entry points) can silently drop code. The post-merge gate catches this before\n997\t   the next wave builds on a broken foundation.\n998\t\n999\t6. **Report completion — spot-check claims first:**\n1000\t\n1001\t   **Wave-close heartbeat (#2410):** after spot-checks finish (pass or fail),\n1002\t   before the `## Wave {N} Complete` summary, emit as a literal line:\n1003\t\n1004\t   ```\n1005\t   [checkpoint] phase {PHASE_NUMBER} wave {N}/{M} complete, {P}/{Q} plans done ({wave_success}/{wave_plan_count} ok)\n1006\t   ```\n1007\t\n1008\t   For each SUMMARY.md:\n1009\t   - Verify first 2 files from `key-files.created` exist on disk\n1010\t   - Check `gsd_run check evaluation-scope --plan \"{phase}-{plan}\" --commits-only --raw` returns `commits` with ≥1 entry (commits on THIS branch only — #5164; a commit that lives only on another branch does not satisfy the check; exit `69` means the scope could not be resolved, which fails the spot-check, never \"no commits yet\")\n1011\t   - Check for `## Self-Check: FAILED` marker\n1012\t\n1013\t   If ANY spot-check fails: report which plan failed, route to failure handler — ask \"Retry plan?\" or \"Continue with remaining waves?\"\n1014\t\n1015\t   If pass:\n1016\t   ```\n1017\t   ---\n1018\t   ## Wave {N} Complete\n1019\t\n1020\t   **{Plan ID}: {Plan Name}**\n1021\t   {What was built — from SUMMARY.md}\n1022\t   {Notable deviations, if any}\n1023\t\n1024\t   {If more waves: what this enables for next wave}\n1025\t   ---\n1026\t   ```\n1027\t\n1028\t7. **Handle failures:**\n1029\t   **Step 7.0 — classify before branching (#3095):**\n1030\t   ```bash\n1031\t   CLASS_JSON=$(gsd_run query agent.classify-failure -- \"$AGENT_RETURN_BODY\")\n1032\t   CLASS=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.class')\n1033\t   SENTINEL=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.sentinel // empty')\n1034\t   RETRY_AFTER=$(echo \"$CLASS_JSON\" | jq -r '.retryAfterSeconds // empty')\n1035\t   if [ -n \"$RETRY_AFTER\" ]; then RETRY_HINT=\"  Provider hinted retry-after: ${RETRY_AFTER}s\"; else RETRY_HINT=\"\"; fi\n1036\t   ```\n1037\t   One classifier branch handles sentinels across Claude/Copilot/Codex/Antigravity. Reference: `docs/research/provider-rate-limit-signals.md`.\n1038\t   **Abnormal ends reconcile first (#4217):** an abnormal session end (`turn_aborted`-class) routes through the step-4 artifact reconciliation BEFORE classifying the failure — artifacts decide.\n1039\t   **Step 7.1 — `class == \"quota-exceeded\"`:** follow the quota-recovery fragment below.\n1040\t   **Step 7.2 — `class == \"classify-handoff-bug\"`:**\n1041\t   If error contains `classifyHandoffIfNeeded is not defined`, treat as Claude runtime bug. Run the same step-5 spot-checks; PASS => treat as success, FAIL => fall through.\n1042\t   **Step 7.3 — `class == \"unknown-failure\"`:**\n1043\t   Report failed plan and ask Continue/Stop; continuing may cascade into dependent plan failures.\n1044\t\n1045\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-quota-recovery.md\n1046\t\n1047\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-between-wave-reset.md\n1048\t\n1049\t8. **Execute checkpoint plans between waves** — see `<checkpoint_handling>`.\n1050\t9. **Proceed to next wave.**\n1051\t</step>\n1052\t<step name=\"checkpoint_handling\">\n1053\tPlans with `autonomous: false` require user interaction.\n1054\t**Auto-mode checkpoint handling:**\n1055\tRead auto-advance config (chain flag OR user preference — same boolean as `check.auto-mode`):\n1056\t```bash\n1057\tAUTO_MODE=$(gsd_run query check auto-mode --pick active 2>/dev/null)\n1058\t```\n1059\t\n1060\tWhen executor returns a checkpoint AND `AUTO_MODE` is `true`:\n1061\t- **human-verify** → Auto-spawn continuation agent with `{user_response}` = `\"approved\"`. Log `⚡ Auto-approved checkpoint`. **Except `blocking-human`.**\n1062\t- **decision** → `auto_select` present: auto-spawn with `{user_response}` = that option, log `⚡ Auto-selected: [option]`. Absent: present to user (#4095). **Except `blocking-human`.**\n1063\t- **human-action** → Present to user (existing behavior below). Auth gates cannot be automated.\n1064\t\n1065\t<!-- gsd:protected -->\n1066\t**Carve-out — overrides all branches above.** If the returned `Gate:` is `blocking-human` (precondition-unmet, #3210), or its `<what-built>` mentions `Package verification required before install` or `Package install failed — human verification required`, never auto-approve or auto-select. Present to user (standard flow). Log `⛔ blocking-human gate — auto-mode suspended`.\n1067\t\n1068\t**Standard flow (not auto-mode, human-action, or blocking-human):**\n1069\t\n1070\t1. Spawn agent for checkpoint plan\n1071\t2. Agent runs until checkpoint task or auth gate → returns structured state\n1072\t3. Agent return includes: completed tasks table, current task + blocker, checkpoint type/details, what's awaited\n1073\t4. **Present to user:**\n1074\t   ```\n1075\t   ## Checkpoint: [Type]\n1076\t\n1077\t   **Plan:** 03-03 Dashboard Layout\n1078\t   **Progress:** 2/3 tasks complete\n1079\t\n1080\t   [Checkpoint Details from agent return]\n1081\t   [Awaiting section from agent return]\n1082\t   ```\n1083\t5. User responds: \"approved\"/\"done\" | issue description | decision selection\n1084\t6. **Spawn continuation agent (NOT resume)** using continuation-prompt.md template:\n1085\t   - `{completed_tasks_table}`: From checkpoint return\n1086\t   - `{resume_task_number}` + `{resume_task_name}`: Current task\n1087\t   - `{user_response}`: What user provided\n1088\t   - `{resume_instructions}`: Based on checkpoint type\n1089\t7. Continuation agent verifies previous commits, continues from resume point\n1090\t8. Repeat until plan completes or user stops\n1091\t\n1092\t**Why fresh agent, not resume:** Resume relies on internal serialization that breaks with parallel tool calls. Fresh agents with explicit state are more reliable.\n1093\t\n1094\t**Checkpoints in parallel waves:** Agent pauses and returns while other parallel agents may complete. Present checkpoint, spawn continuation, wait for all before next wave.\n1095\t</step>\n1096\t\n1097\t<step name=\"aggregate_results\">\n1098\tAfter all waves:\n1099\t\n1100\t```markdown\n1101\t## Phase {X}: {Name} Execution Complete\n1102\t\n1103\t**Waves:** {N} | **Plans:** {M}/{total} complete\n1104\t\n1105\t| Wave | Plans | Status |\n1106\t|------|-------|--------|\n1107\t| 1 | plan-01, plan-02 | ✓ Complete |\n1108\t| CP | plan-03 | ✓ Verified |\n1109\t| 2 | plan-04 | ✓ Complete |\n1110\t\n1111\t### Plan Details\n1112\t1. **03-01**: [one-liner from SUMMARY.md]\n1113\t2. **03-02**: [one-liner from SUMMARY.md]\n1114\t\n1115\t### Issues Encountered\n1116\t[Aggregate from SUMMARYs, or \"None\"]\n1117\t```\n1118\t\n1119\tThe `verify:post` hook dispatch and the SECURITY threats-open gate are the first step of the shared\n1120\tverification step (`verify_post_security_gate` in `verify_phase_goal` below), so verify-work's\n1121\tre-verification route runs them too (#5118).\n1122\t</step>\n1123\t\n1124\tIf `section_manifest` is `null` or `\"partial-wave\"` is in its `included` list: read and execute `gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/partial-wave.md`. Otherwise skip — do not read the file.\n1125\t\n1126\t<step name=\"verify_phase_goal\">\n1127\tVerify phase achieved its GOAL, not just completed tasks: read and execute\n1128\t`gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase/steps/verify-phase-goal.md` — the ONE verification action, the\n1129\twhole sequence (the `verify:post` dispatch with the SECURITY threats-open gate, `code_review_gate`\n1130\twith its TDD escalation, the gap-closure parent-artifact close, the manifest-gated `regression_gate`,\n1131\tthe verifier dispatch, the fingerprint, and the owner's `verification.status` read with stderr\n1132\tkept), shared with verify-work (#5118). If it stopped (TDD block, regression abort, refused\n1133\treport), stop here.\n1134\t\n1135\t**TDD review escalation (#4011):** the `tdd.review-checkpoint` gate is advisory (`blocking: false`)\n1136\texcept when `TDD_MODE=true` AND `GATE_RESULT.block == true` — no MVP condition — where the shared\n1137\tstep escalates the end-of-phase review to blocking: refuse to mark the phase complete and present\n1138\t`Phase blocked: {N} TDD plan(s) violate the RED→GREEN gate sequence under TDD.` Never proceed to\n1139\t`close_parent_artifacts`, `verify_phase_goal`'s verifier or `phase.complete` past that block. Full\n1140\tcontract: `gsd-core/references/execute-mvp-tdd.md` and the step's `code_review_gate`.\n1141\t\n1142\tRoute on `$STATUS`: if `passed`, proceed to update_roadmap. Otherwise keep the phase pending — present `$NEXT_ACTION` to the user and, when `$NEXT_COMMAND` is non-empty, show it as the next command to run. The query covers every case — including no report (`missing`) and no phase directory (`phase_dir_not_found`) — and a status outside the closed set is a hard error the shared step already halted on, so no per-status arm needs to be listed here.\n1143\t\n1144\t**If human_needed:**\n1145\t\n1146\t**Step A: Persist human verification items as UAT file.**\n1147\t\n1148\tCreate `{phase_dir}/{phase_num}-UAT.md` using UAT template format:\n1149\t\n1150\t```markdown\n1151\t---\n1152\tstatus: testing\n1153\tphase: {phase_num}-{phase_name}\n1154\tsource: [{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md]\n1155\tstarted: [now ISO]\n1156\tupdated: [now ISO]\n1157\t---\n1158\t\n1159\t## Current Test\n1160\t\n1161\tnumber: 1\n1162\tname: {first human_verification item description}\n1163\texpected: |\n1164\t  {expected behavior from VERIFICATION.md}\n1165\tawaiting: user response\n1166\t\n1167\t## Tests\n1168\t\n1169\t{For each human_verification item from VERIFICATION.md:}\n1170\t\n1171\t### {N}. {item description}\n1172\texpected: {expected behavior from VERIFICATION.md}\n1173\tresult: [pending]\n1174\t\n1175\t## Summary\n1176\t\n1177\ttotal: {count}\n1178\tpassed: 0\n1179\tissues: 0\n1180\tpending: {count}\n1181\tskipped: 0\n1182\tblocked: 0\n1183\t\n1184\t## Gaps\n1185\t```\n1186\t\n1187\tCommit the file:\n1188\t```bash\n1189\tgsd_run query commit \"test({phase_num}): persist human verification items as UAT\" --files \"{phase_dir}/{phase_num}-UAT.md\"\n1190\t```\n1191\t\n1192\t**Step B: Present to user**:\n1193\t\n1194\t```\n1195\t## ◷ Phase {X}: {Name} — Human Verification Needed\n1196\t\n1197\tAll automated checks passed. {N} item(s) require human testing before this phase can be marked complete:\n1198\t\n1199\t{From VERIFICATION.md human_verification section}\n1200\t\n1201\tTests saved to `{phase_num}-UAT.md`.\n1202\t\n1203\tWhen ready to run the tests:\n1204\t\n1205\t`/gsd-verify-work {X} ${GSD_WS}`\n1206\t\n1207\tVerify-work will walk you through each item and mark the phase complete when all tests pass.\n1208\t```\n1209\t\n1210\t**Do NOT advance the phase from this branch.** Phase completion is handled by verify-work's auto-transition after UAT passes.\n1211\t\n1212\t**If user acknowledges without reporting issues (including \"ok\", \"noted\", \"ack\", \"got it\", \"approved\", \"done\", \"yes\", \"pass\", or similar):** Stop. The phase remains pending. No further orchestrator action — wait for the user to run `/gsd-verify-work`.\n1213\t\n1214\t**If user reports issues now:** Proceed to gap closure.\n1215\t\n1216\t**If gaps_found:**\n1217\t@~/.claude/gsd-core/references/execute-phase-requirement-revert.md\n1218\t```\n1219\t## ⚠ Phase {X}: {Name} — Gaps Found\n1220\t\n1221\t**Score:** {N}/{M} must-haves verified\n1222\t**Report:** {phase_dir}/{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md\n1223\t\n1224\t### What's Missing\n1225\t{Gap summaries from VERIFICATION.md}\n1226\t\n1227\t---\n1228\t## ▶ Next Up — [${PROJECT_CODE}] ${PROJECT_TITLE}\n1229\t\n1230\t`/clear` then:\n1231\t\n1232\t`/gsd-plan-phase {X} --gaps ${GSD_WS}`\n1233\t\n1234\tAlso: `cat {phase_dir}/{phase_num}-VERIFICATION.md` — full report\n1235\tAlso: `/gsd-verify-work {X} ${GSD_WS}` — manual testing first\n1236\t```\n1237\t\n1238\tGap closure cycle: `/gsd-plan-phase {X} --gaps ${GSD_WS}` reads VERIFICATION.md → creates gap plans with `gap_closure: true` → user runs `/gsd-execute-phase {X} --gaps-only ${GSD_WS}` → verifier re-runs.\n1239\t</step>\n1240\t\n1241\tThe `gap-closure-artifacts` section is evaluated inside the shared verification step\n1242\t(`verify_phase_goal` above) — between its code-review gate and its regression gate, where it ran\n1243\tbefore #5118 — gated on this id exactly as every section here is gated.\n1244\t\n1245\tThe `regression-gate` section is evaluated inside the shared verification step (`verify_phase_goal`\n1246\tabove), which gates it on this id exactly as every section here is gated (#5118).\n1247\t\n1248\t<step name=\"update_roadmap\">\n1249\t**Mark phase complete and update all tracking files:**\n1250\t\n1251\t```bash\n1252\tCOMPLETION=$(gsd_run query phase.complete \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")\n1253\t```\n1254\t\n1255\tThe CLI handles:\n1256\t- Marking phase checkbox `[x]` with completion date\n1257\t- Updating Progress table (Status → Complete, date)\n1258\t- Updating plan count to final\n1259\t- Advancing STATE.md to next phase\n1260\t- Updating REQUIREMENTS.md traceability\n1261\t- Scanning for verification debt (returns `warnings` array)\n1262\t\n1263\tExtract from result: `next_phase`, `next_phase_name`, `is_last_phase`, `warnings`, `has_warnings`.\n1264\t\n1265\t**If has_warnings is true**:\n1266\t```\n1267\t## Phase {X} marked complete with {N} warnings:\n1268\t\n1269\t{list each warning}\n1270\t\n1271\tThese items are tracked and will appear in `/gsd-progress` and `/gsd-audit-uat`.\n1272\t```\n1273\t\n1274\t```bash\n1275\tgsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-{X}): complete phase execution\" --files .planning/ROADMAP.md .planning/STATE.md .planning/REQUIREMENTS.md {phase_dir}/*-VERIFICATION.md\n1276\t```\n1277\t</step>\n1278\t\n1279\t<step name=\"auto_copy_learnings\">\n1280\t**Auto-extract and copy phase learnings to global store (when enabled).**\n1281\t\n1282\tThis step runs AFTER phase completion and SUMMARY.md is written. It produces the phase's\n1283\tlearnings artifact (the sole producer is otherwise the user-invoked\n1284\t`/gsd-extract-learnings`) and copies it to the global learnings store at\n1285\t`~/.gsd/knowledge/`.\n1286\t\n1287\t**Check config gate:**\n1288\t```bash\n1289\tGL_ENABLED=$(gsd_run query config-get features.global_learnings --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"false\")\n1290\t```\n1291\t\n1292\t**If `GL_ENABLED` is not `true`:** Skip this step entirely (feature disabled by default).\n1293\t\n1294\t**If enabled:**\n1295\t\n1296\t1. Run the `extract-learnings` workflow for the JUST-COMPLETED phase (its\n1297\t   `write_learnings` step writes `{phase_dir}/{PADDED_PHASE}-LEARNINGS.md`). Extraction\n1298\t   failure must NOT block phase completion — report the failure and continue.\n1299\t2. Copy the phase artifact to the global store:\n1300\t```bash\n1301\tgsd_run query learnings.copy 2>/dev/null || echo \"⚠ Learnings copy failed — continuing\"\n1302\t```\n1303\tCopy failure must NOT block phase completion.\n1304\t</step>\n1305\t\n1306\t<step name=\"close_phase_todos\">\n1307\t**Auto-close todos whose `resolves_phase` matches this phase (#2433)**, after `update_roadmap`.\n1308\t\n1309\t```bash\n1310\tshopt -s nullglob 2>/dev/null; setopt NULL_GLOB 2>/dev/null\n1311\tPENDING_DIR=\".planning/todos/pending\"\n1312\tCOMPLETED_DIR=\".planning/todos/completed\"\n1313\tmkdir -p \"$COMPLETED_DIR\"\n1314\tPHASE_NUM=\"${PHASE_NUMBER}\"\n1315\t#2576\n1316\tnormalize_phase_num() {\n1317\t  printf '%s' \"${1//\\\"/}\" | sed 's/^0*\\([0-9]\\)/\\1/'\n1318\t}\n1319\tPHASE_NUM_NORM=$(normalize_phase_num \"$PHASE_NUM\")\n1320\tCLOSED=()\n1321\tfor TODO_FILE in \"$PENDING_DIR\"/*.md; do\n1322\t  [ -f \"$TODO_FILE\" ] || continue\n1323\t  RP=$(awk '/^---/{c++;next} c==1 && /^resolves_phase:/{print $2;exit} c==2{exit}' \"$TODO_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n1324\t  RP_NORM=$(normalize_phase_num \"$RP\")\n1325\t  [ -n \"$RP_NORM\" ] && [ \"$RP_NORM\" = \"$PHASE_NUM_NORM\" ] || continue\n1326\t  mv \"$TODO_FILE\" \"$COMPLETED_DIR/\"\n1327\t  CLOSED+=(\"$(basename \"$TODO_FILE\")\")\n1328\tdone\n1329\tif [ ${#CLOSED[@]} -gt 0 ]; then\n1330\t  ADDED=(); REMOVED=()\n1331\t  for f in \"${CLOSED[@]}\"; do ADDED+=(\"$COMPLETED_DIR/$f\"); REMOVED+=(\"$PENDING_DIR/$f\"); done\n1332\t  gsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-${PHASE_NUMBER}): close ${#CLOSED[@]} resolved todo(s)\" --files \"${ADDED[@]}\" .planning/STATE.md --files-removed \"${REMOVED[@]}\" || true\n1333\t  echo \"◆ Closed ${#CLOSED[@]} todo(s) for Phase ${PHASE_NUMBER}:\"; printf '  ✓ %s\\n' \"${CLOSED[@]}\"\n1334\tfi\n1335\t```\n1336\t\n1337\tNo matches: skip silently, never blocks.\n1338\t</step>\n1339\t\n1340\t<step name=\"delegate_post_completion_to_transition\">\n1341\t**#1526 — Delegate post-completion to the transition workflow** (parity: the auto-chain\n1342\tpath must run the SAME post-processing as a normal transition). `phase.complete`\n1343\t(`update_roadmap` above) and verification (`verify_phase_goal`) already ran, so invoke\n1344\ttransition in **post-completion mode**: SKIP its `verify_completion` and\n1345\t`update_roadmap_and_state` (re-running `phase.complete` would double-write state) and\n1346\tBEGIN at `evolve_project`, running 