{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYBcuC8Qm5HNBZxnP5Jt9i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<overview>\n2\tPlans execute autonomously. Checkpoints formalize interaction points where human verification or decisions are needed.\n3\t\n4\t**Core principle:** Claude automates everything with CLI/API. Checkpoints are for verification and decisions, not manual work.\n5\t\n6\t**Golden rules:**\n7\t1. **If Claude can run it, Claude runs it** - Never ask user to execute CLI commands, start servers, or run builds\n8\t2. **Claude sets up the verification environment** - Start dev servers, seed databases, configure env vars\n9\t3. **User only does what requires human judgment** - Visual checks, UX evaluation, \"does this feel right?\"\n10\t4. **Secrets come from user, automation comes from Claude** - Ask for API keys, then Claude uses them via CLI\n11\t5. **Auto-mode bypasses verification checkpoints, and decision checkpoints with a declared `auto_select`** — When `workflow._auto_chain_active` or `workflow.auto_advance` is true in config: human-verify auto-approves; a `checkpoint:decision` carrying `auto_select=\"<option-id>\"` auto-selects that named option; a `checkpoint:decision` with NO `auto_select` escalates to a human instead of guessing by position (#4095); human-action still stops (auth gates cannot be automated)\n12\t6. **`gate=\"blocking-human\"` is never auto-approved** — a checkpoint carrying this gate stops for a human in *every* mode, including auto-mode, regardless of its type. Rule 5 does not apply to it. The executor's precondition-unmet checkpoint (a task's `<precondition>` evaluated false — unmet `user_setup` step, missing env var, absent prior-phase artifact) reports this gate (#3210).\n13\t\n14\t**The `gate` attribute:**\n15\t\n16\t| Value | Auto-mode behavior | Use for |\n17\t|-------|--------------------|---------|\n18\t| `gate=\"blocking\"` | Bypassed per rule 5 (human-verify auto-approves; decision auto-selects only when `auto_select` names an option, else escalates) | The default. Post-hoc verification and implementation choices that are safe to take the recommended path on when unattended. |\n19\t| `gate=\"blocking-human\"` | **Never bypassed.** Stops for a human in auto-mode too. | Irreversible or trust-establishing steps a human must actually see: package-legitimacy verification before install, any decision whose default answer would be wrong to assume, and unmet `<precondition>` facts the executor cannot establish on its own (#3210). |\n20\t\n21\tReach for `gate=\"blocking-human\"` whenever auto-approving the checkpoint would defeat its purpose. If the checkpoint exists because a human must *decide* something, `blocking` is the wrong gate — auto-mode will decide it for them.\n22\t\n23\tThe gate spans two layers, and both must honor it. `gsd-executor` refuses to auto-approve a `gate=\"blocking-human\"` checkpoint and escalates it via `checkpoint_return_format` precisely so a human sees it; `execute-phase`'s `checkpoint_handling` step then decides what the user is actually shown. An orchestrator that dispatches on checkpoint *type* alone would auto-approve the very checkpoint the executor just refused to auto-approve, nullifying that refusal one layer up and letting an unattended `--auto` / `--chain` run install a package no human ever vetted.\n24\t</overview>\n25\t\n26\t<checkpoint_types>\n27\t\n28\t<type name=\"human-verify\">\n29\t## checkpoint:human-verify (Most Common - 90%)\n30\t\n31\t**When:** Claude completed automated work, human confirms it works correctly.\n32\t\n33\t> **Default mode (#3309): `workflow.human_verify_mode = end-of-phase`.** New projects do NOT halt mid-flight at *planner-emitted* `checkpoint:human-verify` tasks. (The executor-synthesized **tracer feedback gate** is the one runtime checkpoint this mode also governs, with its own precedence chain — see \"Tracer feedback gate (#3299)\" below.) The planner suppresses those task emissions and embeds the verification details into the relevant `auto` task's `<verify><human-check>` block; the verifier harvests every `<verify><human-check>` at end-of-phase (Step 8) and consolidates them into the existing `human_needed` → `{phase_num}-UAT.md` flow in `workflows/execute-phase.md`. The user reviews everything in one batch.\n34\t>\n35\t> **Why this is the default:** every mid-flight halt costs a full executor cold-start (CLAUDE.md, MEMORY.md, STATE.md, plan re-read on respawn) because subagent context is discarded across the pause. A plan with N human-verify checkpoints pays the cold-start cost N+1 times — measured at \"tens of thousands of tokens\" per round-trip on real projects.\n36\t>\n37\t> Set `workflow.human_verify_mode = mid-flight` in `.planning/config.json` to opt back into the pre-#3309 behavior of halting at every checkpoint. `checkpoint:decision` and `checkpoint:human-action` are unaffected by either value — those gate the work itself, not post-hoc verification.\n38\t\n39\t**Use for:**\n40\t- Visual UI checks (layout, styling, responsiveness)\n41\t- Interactive flows (click through wizard, test user flows)\n42\t- Functional verification (feature works as expected)\n43\t- Audio/video playback quality\n44\t- Animation smoothness\n45\t- Accessibility testing\n46\t\n47\t**Structure:**\n48\t```xml\n49\t<task type=\"checkpoint:human-verify\" gate=\"blocking\">\n50\t  <what-built>[What Claude automated and deployed/built]</what-built>\n51\t  <how-to-verify>\n52\t    [Exact steps to test - URLs, commands, expected behavior]\n53\t  </how-to-verify>\n54\t  <resume-signal>[How to continue - \"approved\", \"yes\", or describe issues]</resume-signal>\n55\t</task>\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t**Example: UI Component (shows key pattern: Claude starts server BEFORE checkpoint)**\n59\t```xml\n60\t<task type=\"auto\">\n61\t  <name>Build responsive dashboard layout</name>\n62\t  <files>src/components/Dashboard.tsx, src/app/dashboard/page.tsx</files>\n63\t  <action>Create dashboard with sidebar, header, and content area. Use Tailwind responsive classes for mobile.</action>\n64\t  <verify>npm run build succeeds, no TypeScript errors</verify>\n65\t  <done>Dashboard component builds without errors</done>\n66\t</task>\n67\t\n68\t<task type=\"auto\">\n69\t  <name>Start dev server for verification</name>\n70\t  <action>Run `npm run dev` in background, wait for \"ready\" message, capture port</action>\n71\t  <verify>fetch http://localhost:3000 returns 200</verify>\n72\t  <done>Dev server running at http://localhost:3000</done>\n73\t</task>\n74\t\n75\t<task type=\"checkpoint:human-verify\" gate=\"blocking\">\n76\t  <what-built>Responsive dashboard layout - dev server running at http://localhost:3000</what-built>\n77\t  <how-to-verify>\n78\t    Visit http://localhost:3000/dashboard and verify:\n79\t    1. Desktop (>1024px): Sidebar left, content right, header top\n80\t    2. Tablet (768px): Sidebar collapses to hamburger menu\n81\t    3. Mobile (375px): Single column layout, bottom nav appears\n82\t    4. No layout shift or horizontal scroll at any size\n83\t  </how-to-verify>\n84\t  <resume-signal>Type \"approved\" or describe layout issues</resume-signal>\n85\t</task>\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\t**Example: Xcode Build**\n89\t```xml\n90\t<task type=\"auto\">\n91\t  <name>Build macOS app with Xcode</name>\n92\t  <files>App.xcodeproj, Sources/</files>\n93\t  <action>Run `xcodebuild -project App.xcodeproj -scheme App build`. Check for compilation errors in output.</action>\n94\t  <verify>Build output contains \"BUILD SUCCEEDED\", no errors</verify>\n95\t  <done>App builds successfully</done>\n96\t</task>\n97\t\n98\t<task type=\"checkpoint:human-verify\" gate=\"blocking\">\n99\t  <what-built>Built macOS app at DerivedData/Build/Products/Debug/App.app</what-built>\n100\t  <how-to-verify>\n101\t    Open App.app and test:\n102\t    - App launches without crashes\n103\t    - Menu bar icon appears\n104\t    - Preferences window opens correctly\n105\t    - No visual glitches or layout issues\n106\t  </how-to-verify>\n107\t  <resume-signal>Type \"approved\" or describe issues</resume-signal>\n108\t</task>\n109\t```\n110\t\n111\t### Tracer feedback gate (#3299)\n112\t\n113\tA `type=\"tracer\"` task is followed by an early integration checkpoint on the proven slice, run BEFORE any expansion task. This checkpoint is **synthesized by the executor at runtime** — no planner emits it — so planner-side `human_verify_mode` suppression cannot reach it. It must therefore consult the mode itself.\n114\t\n115\tEvaluate the rows **in order** and take the first that matches — they are a precedence chain, not independent conditions:\n116\t\n117\t| # | Run | Tracer `<verify>` | Behavior |\n118\t|---|---|---|---|\n119\t| 1 | **Any run, any mode** (incl. auto) | task carries `gate=\"blocking-human\"` | **STOP → `checkpoint:human-verify`.** Never auto-continued. |\n120\t| 2 | Auto mode active (`AUTO_CHAIN`/`AUTO_CFG`) | any (row 1 already took `blocking-human`) | Re-run verify; HALT on failure, continue on success. **Pre-existing behavior — unchanged by #3299.** |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015uqDvbhWLoQtByVfv2JsmW","agent_id":"a6c93c843462481eb","session_id":"uuid-7","uuid":"uuid-206","timestamp":"2026-10-07T19:02:02.952Z","subagent_type":"gsd-executor","task_description":"Execute plan 01 of phase 01"}
